    "reason": "[ev-270c9e3fe130] and the computed CRD diff only show that ManagedResourceDefinition v1alpha1 is a new CRD in the target release. Its excerpt is empty, and no upstream text says that anything fails, is rejected or must be migrated if the CRD is missing. The generic \"install or update CRDs\" line comes from the computed diff, not from upstream text. \"The new resource type will not be available\" describes a new feature that is unavailable, not a broken workload, so migration-required over-claims mandatory work. To decide between none and a failure kind, we need release notes or an upgrade guide saying whether Crossplane, or anything else that already works, fails without this CRD.",
